{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide", "label": "NFR Design Guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_resilience_patterns", "label": "Resilience Pattern Selection Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Resilience Patterns", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Six patterns chosen by failure-mode analysis with concrete starting configuration: circuit breaker (threshold 5, timeout 30s), bulkhead per dependency, retry with exponential backoff plus jitter, timeout on every external call without exception, fallback when degraded mode beats total failure, rate limiter to shield downstream from upstream bursts."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_circuit_breaker_state_machine", "label": "Circuit Breaker State Machine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Circuit Breaker State Machine", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closed counts failures and opens at threshold; Open fails fast without calling downstream; Half-Open probes with a single request and closes on success or re-opens on failure - failing fast is the point, since queuing calls to a dead dependency is what propagates the outage."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_caching_architecture", "label": "Cache Placement Decision Matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Caching Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Placement, TTL and invalidation are chosen together per scenario (CDN edge with version-hash URLs, gateway with event-driven purge, application cache write-through/behind, session store with explicit delete). Never cache data that must be strongly consistent, always set a TTL because unbounded caches become stale data stores, and target above 90% hit ratio on read-heavy paths."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_scalability_patterns", "label": "Horizontal Scaling Strategies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Scalability Patterns", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stateless services, sharding, read replicas (above 10:1 read:write, accepting replication lag), event-driven decoupling, and CQRS. Shard keys need high cardinality, even distribution, query locality and immutability, because changing a shard key forces a data migration."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_sli_slo_definition", "label": "SLI/SLO and Error Budget Definition", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Reliability Engineering", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SLIs are ratios (successful/total, below-threshold/total, correct/total), SLOs state a target over a window, and the error budget is 1 minus the SLO - 99.9% is 43.2 minutes of downtime per 30 days, which converts an abstract target into a spendable allowance."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_failure_mode_checklist", "label": "Failure Mode Checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Failure Mode Checklist", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per component: what happens on unavailability, doubled response time, over-capacity throughput, and corrupted dependency data; is there a graceful degradation path; what is the blast radius (user, tenant, region, global); and what is the recovery procedure. Blast radius and recovery are asked explicitly so they are designed rather than discovered."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_nfr_to_architecture_mapping", "label": "NFR-to-Architecture Mapping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "NFR-to-Architecture Mapping", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each quantified NFR is translated into concrete structure - sub-100ms latency into caching and async non-blocking I/O, 99.9% availability into multi-AZ plus health checks plus circuit breakers, RTO under an hour into multi-region active-passive with tested runbooks, zero-downtime deploys into blue-green or canary with backward-compatible migrations."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_resilience_patterns", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Resilience Patterns", "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architect_agent_nfr_design_guide_circuit_breaker_state_machine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-architect-agent/nfr-design-guide.md", "source_location": "Circuit Breaker State Machine", "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_architec